WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:27.170
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
01:27.440 --> 01:34.910
[The Great Long March]

3
01:35.370 --> 01:37.670
[Episode 46]

4
01:38.440 --> 01:42.229
[Panzhou, Sichuan]

5
01:38.509 --> 01:41.400
Comrade Peng Dehuai was worried I'd fall,

6
01:41.600 --> 01:43.759
so he stood on the opposite bank like this,

7
01:43.759 --> 01:44.840
ready to catch me.

8
01:45.120 --> 01:48.229
As a result, I bumped into him and almost knocked him over.

9
01:48.229 --> 01:51.430
This bump actually made him laugh.

10
01:52.070 --> 01:54.789
He said he didn't expect a Commander-in-Chief like me

11
01:52.800 --> 01:55.490
[Xu Xiangqian, Commander-in-Chief of the Red Army Frontline General Headquarters and of the 4th Front Army]

12
01:54.870 --> 01:56.789
to be so good at ziplining.

13
01:55.590 --> 01:59.780
[Li Xiannian, Political Commissar of the 30th Red Army]

14
01:59.070 --> 02:00.120
I told him,

15
02:00.200 --> 02:02.990
everyone has a first time for everything.

16
02:06.400 --> 02:09.389
Then what else did you talk about?

17
02:09.919 --> 02:11.320
Comrade Peng Dehuai said

18
02:11.350 --> 02:12.790
he was a Corps Commander,

19
02:13.200 --> 02:15.110
and I was the Commander-in-Chief of the Front Army.

20
02:15.110 --> 02:17.829
He should have come to see me instead.

21
02:18.480 --> 02:19.790
But I felt

22
02:21.000 --> 02:22.390
we were all family.

23
02:22.670 --> 02:24.160
Why speak like strangers?

24
02:24.829 --> 02:26.290
Why draw a line between us?

25
02:26.440 --> 02:28.280
That's what I thought myself.

26
02:30.480 --> 02:31.630
To be honest,

27
02:32.200 --> 02:35.060
that was my first time meeting Comrade Peng Dehuai.

28
02:35.390 --> 02:36.510
I don't know why,

29
02:36.510 --> 02:38.160
but it felt like we had known each other for a long time.

30
02:38.160 --> 02:40.160
We had endless things to talk about.

31
02:40.950 --> 02:42.110
We just kept talking.

32
02:42.110 --> 02:44.040
I don't know how long we talked,

33
02:45.440 --> 02:46.720
but we talked a lot.

34
02:48.280 --> 02:49.280
A lot.

35
02:51.320 --> 02:52.320
You see,

36
02:53.920 --> 02:55.440
in just a few short days,

37
02:55.510 --> 02:57.160
so much has happened.

38
02:58.280 --> 02:59.320
It's like,

39
03:02.670 --> 03:04.600
like having a dream.

40
03:05.070 --> 03:06.600
If only it were a dream.

41
03:06.670 --> 03:08.600
Then everything would be all right

42
03:09.350 --> 03:10.630
when we woke up.

43
03:16.950 --> 03:18.210
Commander-in-Chief,

44
03:18.440 --> 03:19.920
I am a revolutionary soldier.

45
03:19.920 --> 03:21.230
Of course, I must obey orders.

46
03:21.230 --> 03:24.070
But there is something I must say.

47
03:25.350 --> 03:26.950
I used to be a carpenter.

48
03:27.200 --> 03:28.550
Before starting work,

49
03:28.790 --> 03:31.630
you need to snap the chalk line accurately and straight.

50
03:31.630 --> 03:33.790
If the chalk line is crooked,

51
03:34.000 --> 03:35.790
the work cannot be done.

52
03:37.440 --> 03:40.110
If we really don't follow the Central Committee,

53
03:40.110 --> 03:42.510
how can we explain it to the soldiers

54
03:42.550 --> 03:44.310
and the cadres?

55
03:57.600 --> 04:00.000
The chalk line is in our own hands.

56
04:00.130 --> 04:01.660
We must not snap it crooked.

57
04:11.480 --> 04:12.350
Xiannian.

58
04:13.200 --> 04:14.630
Today is the 15th day of the 8th lunar month, isn't it?

59
04:14.630 --> 04:15.480
Yes.

60
04:18.190 --> 04:19.790
The moon is so round.

61
04:20.720 --> 04:22.780
I wonder where the Central Committee

62
04:22.920 --> 04:24.520
has reached now.

63
04:27.840 --> 04:29.870
Just as the Central Committee led the 1st Red Army,

64
04:29.870 --> 04:33.200
the 3rd Red Army, and the Military Commission Column north,

65
04:33.360 --> 04:36.920
Zhang Guotao, on September 13, 1935,

66
04:37.190 --> 04:40.080
convened a meeting at Kirti Monastery in Aba, Sichuan,

67
04:40.080 --> 04:42.960
of the Sichuan-Xikang Provincial Committee of the CPC

68
04:42.960 --> 04:45.290
and Party activists in the 4th Front Army.

69
04:45.400 --> 04:48.080
He incited some cadres who didn't know the truth,

70
04:48.080 --> 04:49.790
slandering the Central Committee's insistence on going north

71
04:49.790 --> 04:52.400
as "opportunism" and "rightist flightism".

72
04:52.520 --> 04:54.550
He launched a massive attack on Zhu De, Liu Bocheng,

73
04:54.550 --> 04:58.280
and others who supported the Central Committee's policy of going north.

74
04:58.280 --> 05:01.110
Zhang Guotao publicly distorted the facts

75
05:01.230 --> 05:03.310
about the differences within the Party.

76
05:03.310 --> 05:05.280
He is using the unaware,

77
05:05.280 --> 05:06.600
simple officers and soldiers,

78
05:06.600 --> 05:09.600
and inciting them against the Central Committee's political line.

79
05:09.600 --> 05:11.480
Comrades Dong Zhentang, Chen Bojun,

80
05:11.480 --> 05:12.960
Peng Shaohui, and others

81
05:13.040 --> 05:15.480
were all framed and set up by Zhang Guotao.

82
05:16.550 --> 05:19.550
Especially Comrade Hu Di, Section Chief of the Headquarters Reconnaissance.

83
05:19.550 --> 05:21.400
Because he publicly opposed Zhang Guotao,

84
05:21.400 --> 05:23.730
he was framed with an unwarranted charge.

85
05:23.750 --> 05:25.350
He was accused of being a Kuomintang spy

86
05:25.350 --> 05:26.750
and a counter-revolutionary.

87
05:26.750 --> 05:28.640
He was arrested inexplicably,

88
05:26.820 --> 05:29.340
[Kang Keqing, Zhu De's wife]

89
05:29.220 --> 05:31.350
and I heard he has already been killed.

90
05:31.640 --> 05:34.430
Comrade Hu Di had been operating undercover behind enemy lines for many years,

91
05:34.430 --> 05:35.840
and made great contributions to the Party.

92
05:35.840 --> 05:39.570
That was just a case of making up charges to pin the blame on someone.

93
05:42.600 --> 05:43.640
Bocheng,

94
05:44.640 --> 05:45.310
the top priority

95
05:45.310 --> 05:46.640
is still to work separately

96
05:46.640 --> 05:49.100
to talk to our comrades in the 1st Front Army.

97
05:49.230 --> 05:50.230
We must tell them

98
05:50.480 --> 05:52.790
that our principle of being of one mind with the Central Committee remains unchanged.

99
05:52.790 --> 05:55.430
But we must take the overall situation into consideration

100
05:55.430 --> 05:57.920
and pay attention to our work strategies and methods.

101
05:57.920 --> 05:59.920
The truth will eventually come to light.

102
05:59.920 --> 06:01.600
We cannot make unnecessary sacrifices.

103
06:01.600 --> 06:02.280
Okay.

104
06:03.430 --> 06:05.480
I'll go find Comrade Dong Zhentang right now.

105
06:05.480 --> 06:06.840
Step aside. We want to talk to Zhu De.

106
06:06.840 --> 06:07.600
Step aside.

107
06:07.640 --> 06:08.640
Where is Zhu De?

108
06:08.870 --> 06:09.750
Where is Zhu De?

109
06:09.920 --> 06:10.670
What're you doing?

110
06:10.670 --> 06:12.160
We want an explanation from Zhu De.

111
06:12.160 --> 06:13.400
What exactly do you want?

112
06:13.400 --> 06:14.750
Comrade Kang Keqing.

113
06:19.600 --> 06:20.860
Don't misunderstand.

114
06:21.870 --> 06:25.070
We are here to discuss work with the Commander-in-Chief.

115
06:25.960 --> 06:27.390
Comrade Bocheng, you're here, too.

116
06:27.390 --> 06:30.180
Are you having a private meeting?

117
06:32.159 --> 06:32.870
Kang.

118
06:36.230 --> 06:37.230
Comrade Guotao,

119
06:37.400 --> 06:38.840
if you want to discuss work,

120
06:38.840 --> 06:39.570
that's fine,

121
06:39.670 --> 06:43.140
but there's no need to make such a big scene.

122
06:44.080 --> 06:46.580
I have been in the military for over 20 years.

123
06:47.080 --> 06:48.680
I'm not intimidated by this.

124
06:54.040 --> 06:54.840
Everyone out.

125
06:58.840 --> 07:00.840
I didn't want to bring them here,

126
07:02.110 --> 07:03.600
but some comrades...

127
07:04.430 --> 07:05.490
How should I put it?

128
07:06.350 --> 07:08.010
They have some issues with you

129
07:08.110 --> 07:09.910
and want to know where you stand.

130
07:10.400 --> 07:12.160
About what?

131
07:14.520 --> 07:15.980
Come on, Comrade Bocheng,

132
07:16.010 --> 07:16.670
please sit.

133
07:18.600 --> 07:21.550
This was passed at the meeting this afternoon,

134
07:21.670 --> 07:24.430
the "Resolution on the Struggle Against Right Opportunism".

135
07:24.430 --> 07:25.750
Everyone unanimously agreed

136
07:25.750 --> 07:27.350
that the Central Committee's decision to go north

137
07:27.350 --> 07:29.110
is an act of right escapism

138
07:29.190 --> 07:30.430
and is wrong.

139
07:31.840 --> 07:33.100
Commander-in-Chief,

140
07:33.190 --> 07:35.220
I just want a straight answer from you.

141
07:35.220 --> 07:37.310
Are you in favor of going north

142
07:37.960 --> 07:39.060
or going south?

143
07:42.310 --> 07:43.520
On this issue,

144
07:44.480 --> 07:46.190
I have already made it very clear.

145
07:46.190 --> 07:49.550
The Central Committee's decision to go north is correct.

146
07:49.790 --> 07:50.870
I voted in favor of

147
07:51.040 --> 07:52.600
the Central Committee's resolution

148
07:52.600 --> 07:54.330
at the Lianghekou Conference.

149
07:54.640 --> 07:55.790
Comrade Guotao,

150
07:56.920 --> 07:58.310
you voted in favor too.

151
07:58.430 --> 08:00.040
We can't go back on our word.

152
08:01.430 --> 08:03.080
The Lianghekou Conference.

153
08:04.690 --> 08:05.710
[Huang Chao, Secretary-General of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission,]

154
08:05.190 --> 08:06.720
They call it a Central Committee resolution,

155
08:05.710 --> 08:06.730
[Secretary-General of the Sichuan-Shaanxi Provincial Soviet Government]

156
08:06.840 --> 08:08.430
but many comrades know

157
08:08.550 --> 08:11.720
it was really Mao Zedong's own idea.

158
08:12.040 --> 08:13.600
Don't twist things around.

159
08:14.230 --> 08:18.030
Comrade Mao Zedong is a member of the Politburo Standing Committee.

160
08:18.430 --> 08:20.720
He made a proposal at a Politburo meeting,

161
08:20.720 --> 08:23.160
and the meeting discussed and approved it.

162
08:24.570 --> 08:25.900
What's wrong with that?

163
08:27.310 --> 08:30.240
Don't keep bringing up organizational procedures.

164
08:30.960 --> 08:33.429
I chaired the 1st National Congress of the Party.

165
08:33.429 --> 08:36.230
I was the Party's first Director of Organization.

166
08:36.429 --> 08:38.830
You hadn't even joined the Party back then.

167
08:38.830 --> 08:39.960
The following year,

168
08:40.070 --> 08:41.240
you went to Shanghai

169
08:41.240 --> 08:43.070
and asked Chen Duxiu to let you join the Party.

170
08:43.070 --> 08:44.430
He turned you down.

171
08:44.790 --> 08:45.920
I was right there.

172
08:48.040 --> 08:49.300
I'm getting off track.

173
08:49.880 --> 08:51.210
Let's leave that aside.

174
08:52.880 --> 08:54.430
Let's talk about you and Mao Zedong.

175
08:54.430 --> 08:56.790
Zhu-Mao. Zhu-Mao.

176
08:58.120 --> 08:58.920
Everyone knows

177
08:58.920 --> 09:00.830
how close you and Mao Zedong are.

178
09:01.160 --> 09:03.220
Of course you'll do whatever he says.

179
09:06.000 --> 09:07.240
You're right.

180
09:07.360 --> 09:08.880
Mao and I have been together

181
09:08.880 --> 09:10.950
ever since we joined forces at Jinggang Mountain.

182
09:10.950 --> 09:12.280
We've never been apart.

183
09:12.430 --> 09:13.950
Even Chiang Kai-shek knows

184
09:13.950 --> 09:15.210
we're on the same side.

185
09:15.360 --> 09:16.310
So tell me,

186
09:16.760 --> 09:19.430
how could I possibly oppose Mao?

187
09:19.470 --> 09:21.470
That doesn't mean you should follow him blindly.

188
09:21.470 --> 09:22.420
All you ever say is Mao Zedong this,

189
09:22.420 --> 09:23.750
Mao Zedong that.

190
09:23.830 --> 09:25.240
Where does that leave you, Zhu De?

191
09:25.240 --> 09:26.040
Exactly!

192
09:26.070 --> 09:27.430
Zhu De, you're just blindly following him.

193
09:27.430 --> 09:29.030
Isn't that blind obedience?

194
09:29.360 --> 09:30.820
That's exactly what it is!

195
09:30.950 --> 09:32.070
Blind obedience!

196
09:32.070 --> 09:33.360
Where does that leave you, Zhu De?

197
09:33.360 --> 09:35.520
That's blind obedience!

198
09:36.160 --> 09:37.000
Comrades.

199
09:37.160 --> 09:37.830
Comrades!

200
09:37.830 --> 09:38.470
Exactly.

201
09:39.070 --> 09:40.400
Mao and I

202
09:40.470 --> 09:42.200
haven't always seen eye to eye.

203
09:43.950 --> 09:46.210
After we left Jinggang Mountain in 1929,

204
09:46.830 --> 09:49.920
we had some very heated arguments.

205
09:50.070 --> 09:53.130
Mao even left the Fourth Red Army over our differences.

206
09:53.160 --> 09:55.550
But later events proved him right.

207
09:55.640 --> 09:58.590
He was right on a series of

208
09:58.670 --> 10:00.040
major issues that followed.

209
10:00.040 --> 10:01.640
He convinced me completely.

210
10:02.120 --> 10:04.250
How can you call that blind obedience?

211
10:05.760 --> 10:06.790
Comrade Guotao,

212
10:07.090 --> 10:08.900
let me share something

213
10:09.160 --> 10:11.410
we learned at the Zunyi Conference.

214
10:12.920 --> 10:14.950
We should follow

215
10:15.160 --> 10:16.770
whoever holds the truth.

216
10:18.040 --> 10:18.920
What's more,

217
10:19.030 --> 10:22.190
the decision to march north and fight the Japanese was made collectively by the Central Committee.

218
10:22.190 --> 10:24.850
Our Red Army has always followed one principle:

219
10:25.040 --> 10:27.100
The Party commands the armed forces.

220
10:29.920 --> 10:32.670
Then let me share something I learnt, too.

221
10:33.430 --> 10:36.030
Following a Central Committee bent on fleeing

222
10:36.470 --> 10:40.430
will only lead to our downfall sooner or later.

223
10:42.550 --> 10:43.710
Downfall?

224
10:44.880 --> 10:47.520
Back when we were at Jinggang Mountain,

225
10:48.040 --> 10:51.240
many people said we were doomed.

226
10:51.360 --> 10:53.430
But not only did we survive,

227
10:53.470 --> 10:56.190
we also established a vast Central Soviet Area.

228
10:56.670 --> 10:57.470
That proves

229
10:57.640 --> 10:59.820
our strategic approach was right.

230
11:01.830 --> 11:03.090
That's just an excuse.

231
11:03.280 --> 11:04.520
We won't accept it.

232
11:04.710 --> 11:06.550
That's right! We won't accept it!

233
11:06.550 --> 11:07.240
That's just an excuse!

234
11:07.240 --> 11:08.190
We oppose marching north!

235
11:08.190 --> 11:09.400
Marching south is the right choice!

236
11:09.400 --> 11:11.360
Marching south is the right choice!

237
11:11.360 --> 11:12.360
Marching north is an act of retreat!

238
11:12.360 --> 11:13.290
Down with Zhu De!

239
11:13.470 --> 11:17.950
Down with Zhu De!

240
11:17.950 --> 11:19.520
Who are you trying to bring down?

241
11:19.520 --> 11:20.640
Who?

242
11:22.120 --> 11:23.190
Who were shouting just now?

243
11:23.190 --> 11:24.310
Step forward!

244
11:24.430 --> 11:26.000
Did you come here to discuss work?

245
11:26.000 --> 11:27.910
Are you even Red Army cadres?

246
11:28.760 --> 11:30.250
You want to bring down Zhu De?

247
11:30.250 --> 11:32.240
Bring down the Commander-in-Chief of our Red Army?

248
11:32.240 --> 11:33.590
I'd like to see you try!

249
11:49.520 --> 11:50.780
Commander-in-Chief.

250
11:52.760 --> 11:55.160
I came here to discuss work with you.

251
11:55.400 --> 11:57.520
But how are we supposed to resolve anything

252
11:57.520 --> 11:59.180
when you're acting like this?

253
12:00.400 --> 12:01.430
How about this?

254
12:04.640 --> 12:06.880
I have another document here.

255
12:07.950 --> 12:09.240
I took the liberty

256
12:09.640 --> 12:11.520
of drafting it

257
12:11.640 --> 12:13.310
in both our names.

258
12:13.430 --> 12:17.670
It's called the "Political Guarantee Plan for a Major Southern Offensive."

259
12:17.670 --> 12:18.760
I've decided to issue it

260
12:18.760 --> 12:21.430
in the name of the Red Army General Political Department.

261
12:21.430 --> 12:22.690
Commander-in-Chief,

262
12:22.710 --> 12:24.160
for the sake of the bigger picture,

263
12:24.160 --> 12:26.910
I implore you

264
12:28.550 --> 12:29.730
to sign it.

265
12:36.240 --> 12:37.240
The two of us?

266
12:40.230 --> 12:41.420
Which two of us?

267
12:45.040 --> 12:46.300
Comrade Zhang Guotao,

268
12:47.790 --> 12:49.550
let me make this perfectly clear.

269
12:49.550 --> 12:50.520
I will not sign

270
12:50.630 --> 12:51.960
this document.

271
12:52.760 --> 12:55.190
And as for the documents you've previously issued

272
12:55.190 --> 12:58.710
in your name and mine without my consent,

273
12:58.710 --> 13:00.440
I do not recognize them either.

274
13:00.640 --> 13:02.370
Let me remind you of something.

275
13:02.760 --> 13:04.960
Going against the Party's directives,

276
13:05.040 --> 13:06.520
disregarding the bigger picture,

277
13:06.520 --> 13:08.280
and pursuing your own agenda,

278
13:08.640 --> 13:10.840
that's what will lead to your downfall.

279
13:12.880 --> 13:14.710
Comrade Guotao, think about it.

280
13:15.180 --> 13:16.570
When the time comes,

281
13:17.380 --> 13:18.970
what will you do?

282
13:30.550 --> 13:32.160
As the old saying goes,

283
13:32.830 --> 13:34.310
three strikes and you're out.

284
13:34.310 --> 13:37.320
I've already done everything I can to accommodate you.

285
13:37.320 --> 13:39.970
Comrade Zhu De, have you thought about this?

286
13:41.190 --> 13:42.880
What if you push me too far?

287
13:47.360 --> 13:48.960
What if you push them too far?

288
13:50.470 --> 13:53.250
What will you do when that happens?

289
15:13.040 --> 15:15.590
In mid-September 1935,

290
15:16.360 --> 15:18.040
on Zhang Guotao's orders,

291
15:18.360 --> 15:21.280
the 4th Front Army units within the Right Route Army,

292
15:21.280 --> 15:23.360
along with some publicity personnel from the 1st Front Army

293
15:23.360 --> 15:26.090
who had been unable to rejoin their units in time,

294
15:26.140 --> 15:27.400
retraced their steps,

295
15:27.460 --> 15:28.640
heading from north to south

296
15:28.640 --> 15:31.040
across the Songpan Grasslands once again.

297
15:31.960 --> 15:34.620
It was autumn, and the weather was turning cold.

298
15:35.000 --> 15:37.280
The officers and soldiers lacked adequate clothing and food.

299
15:37.280 --> 15:40.880
Conditions were even harsher than during their first crossing.

300
15:40.950 --> 15:41.580
At this point,

301
15:41.580 --> 15:42.680
it had been barely more than 20 days

302
15:42.680 --> 15:46.170
since their previous crossing of the grasslands.

303
15:51.400 --> 15:55.330
[Zhang Side, Soldier of the 4th Front Army]

304
16:06.710 --> 16:07.640
Zhang Side.

305
16:07.880 --> 16:09.410
It's dangerous over there!

306
16:09.430 --> 16:10.360
Come back!

307
16:17.640 --> 16:18.520
Squad Leader!

308
16:19.760 --> 16:20.950
I'm back again.

309
16:23.120 --> 16:24.460
I'll be back soon.

310
16:26.490 --> 16:28.370
You've been here for 22 days.

311
16:29.400 --> 16:30.670
Are you cold?

312
16:31.160 --> 16:32.020
Are you hungry?

313
16:33.300 --> 16:34.630
Squad Leader, I'm cold.

314
16:35.590 --> 16:36.950
I'm hungry.

315
16:38.050 --> 16:39.250
Squad Leader.

316
16:40.670 --> 16:41.900
You must be wondering

317
16:42.550 --> 16:43.760
why I came back again.

318
16:44.880 --> 16:46.140
Weren't we supposed to

319
16:46.430 --> 16:50.430
march north with the Central Red Army to fight the Japanese?

320
16:51.550 --> 16:53.120
Just think back to when we

321
16:53.520 --> 16:54.880
joined forces.

322
16:55.490 --> 16:56.900
We were so happy.

323
16:57.310 --> 16:58.310
We had reunions

324
16:58.400 --> 16:59.460
and celebrations.

325
17:01.150 --> 17:02.750
It's only been 3 months.

326
17:03.430 --> 17:05.160
How did things end up like this?

327
17:06.270 --> 17:08.470
Squad Leader, I just don't understand.

328
17:08.640 --> 17:10.670
I... I feel so heavy-hearted.

329
17:16.270 --> 17:19.079
This is my former squad leader.

330
17:19.880 --> 17:22.060
He got trapped here

331
17:22.990 --> 17:25.319
when we crossed the grasslands last time.

332
17:31.560 --> 17:32.880
Comrade Zhang Side,

333
17:33.950 --> 17:35.120
I heard everything

334
17:35.560 --> 17:37.030
you just said.

335
17:42.470 --> 17:43.640
Actually,

336
17:44.730 --> 17:46.450
this military cap I'm wearing

337
17:47.360 --> 17:48.840
isn't mine either.

338
17:51.060 --> 17:52.790
During the Xiang River Battle,

339
17:54.510 --> 17:56.170
I was wounded and fell behind.

340
17:57.030 --> 17:58.690
The enemy was hunting me down,

341
17:58.800 --> 18:00.520
and I didn't know where to go.

342
18:02.750 --> 18:03.800
But later,

343
18:04.360 --> 18:05.600
I came across

344
18:06.990 --> 18:09.050
a group of wounded comrades in a cave.

345
18:09.750 --> 18:12.010
They had formed an Independent Company.

346
18:13.430 --> 18:14.670
This cap

347
18:16.750 --> 18:20.750
was given to me by their company commander, Peng Guangwen.

348
18:22.240 --> 18:24.470
He and the other comrades in the Independent Company

349
18:24.470 --> 18:26.470
entrusted me with their roster

350
18:27.160 --> 18:29.560
and asked me to catch up with the main force.

351
18:29.750 --> 18:31.840
So I set off alone.

352
18:32.390 --> 18:33.650
I kept moving forward,

353
18:34.120 --> 18:35.510
never stopping,

354
18:36.430 --> 18:38.830
asking everywhere for news of the Red Army.

355
18:38.880 --> 18:41.540
I made inquiries while pursuing the main force,

356
18:42.670 --> 18:46.370
and finally caught up with the main force in Zunyi.

357
18:48.030 --> 18:49.560
I had completed my mission.

358
18:50.470 --> 18:53.880
From that moment on, I swore

359
18:54.270 --> 18:56.270
that no matter how difficult things got,

360
18:56.270 --> 18:58.600
I would keep marching with the Red Army.

361
19:00.750 --> 19:02.600
I would never fall behind again.

362
19:13.840 --> 19:14.800
Squad Leader.

363
19:16.560 --> 19:17.600
Sleep on.

364
19:19.650 --> 19:20.650
I'm leaving.

365
19:24.320 --> 19:25.160
Come on.

366
19:31.160 --> 19:31.950
Let's go.

367
19:44.770 --> 19:47.870
[Moscow]

368
19:56.030 --> 19:57.400
I've been entrusted by the CPC Central Committee

369
19:57.400 --> 19:58.880
to report on the Long March of the Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army

370
19:58.880 --> 19:59.990
and explain the significance of the Zunyi Conference

371
19:59.990 --> 20:01.160
to the Comintern.

372
20:01.160 --> 20:02.270
So I really hope

373
20:02.270 --> 20:04.120
to meet Comrade Wang Ming as soon as possible.

374
20:04.120 --> 20:06.720
Comrade Chen Yun, Comrade Wang Ming is inside.

375
20:21.840 --> 20:22.790
Comrade Wang Ming.

376
20:22.680 --> 20:25.500
[Wang Ming, Head of the CPC Delegation to the Comintern]

377
20:24.600 --> 20:25.640
Comrade Chen Yun.

378
20:29.080 --> 20:29.880
Thank you.

379
20:30.510 --> 20:32.950
Comrade Chen Yun, you must have had a long and difficult journey.

380
20:32.950 --> 20:33.750
Not at all.

381
20:35.400 --> 20:36.860
This is Comrade Lin Yuying

382
20:36.880 --> 20:38.400
from our CPC Delegation

383
20:38.430 --> 20:39.470
to the Comintern.

384
20:39.640 --> 20:41.160
Nice to meet you, Comrade Yuying.

385
20:41.100 --> 20:43.060
[Lin Yuying, Member of the CPC Delegation to the Comintern]

386
20:41.210 --> 20:42.840
Hello, Comrade Chen Yun.

387
20:42.920 --> 20:43.560
Good.

388
20:43.600 --> 20:44.750
Comrade Chen Yun, have a seat.

389
20:44.750 --> 20:45.400
Come, have a seat.

390
20:45.400 --> 20:46.330
Please sit down.

391
20:49.270 --> 20:51.360
We've been out of contact with our comrades back home

392
20:51.360 --> 20:53.030
for a full year now.

393
20:53.160 --> 20:55.670
Please bring us up to speed

394
20:55.880 --> 21:00.120
on the current situation of the Party Central Committee and the Red Army.

395
21:00.510 --> 21:01.670
Tell us as much as you can.

396
21:01.670 --> 21:02.510
All right.

397
21:03.560 --> 21:04.960
Since October last year,

398
21:04.990 --> 21:06.650
we began our strategic shift.

399
21:06.710 --> 21:09.270
Following the instructions of the Comintern,

400
21:09.270 --> 21:11.640
we headed for western Hunan.

401
21:12.030 --> 21:13.190
After breaking through

402
21:13.190 --> 21:15.360
several Kuomintang blockades in succession,

403
21:15.360 --> 21:16.560
the enemy discovered

404
21:16.710 --> 21:18.030
our marching plans.

405
21:17.780 --> 21:20.720
[Chen Yun, Member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Politburo]

406
21:18.190 --> 21:19.560
The enemy had set up a tight blockade

407
21:19.560 --> 21:20.820
along the Xiang River,

408
21:20.880 --> 21:23.880
waiting for the Red Army to walk right into their trap.

409
21:24.950 --> 21:26.490
Under these circumstances,

410
21:26.490 --> 21:27.790
Comrade Li De, the Comintern military adviser

411
21:27.790 --> 21:30.200
in charge of military command,

412
21:30.360 --> 21:33.400
and Comrade Bo Gu, who was then in overall charge of the Central Committee,

413
21:33.400 --> 21:36.080
rejected the suggestions made by Mao Zedong and other comrades

414
21:36.080 --> 21:38.510
and insisted on forcing a crossing of the Xiang River.

415
21:38.510 --> 21:41.880
This resulted in devastating losses.

416
21:42.950 --> 21:45.510
While the Central Committee was locked

417
21:45.510 --> 21:47.080
in a struggle with Zhang Guotao

418
21:47.080 --> 21:49.140
over whether to march north or south,

419
21:49.400 --> 21:51.360
after several twists and turns, Chen Yun

420
21:51.360 --> 21:54.330
finally arrived in Moscow in early September.

421
21:55.920 --> 21:57.750
In his briefing to Wang Ming,

422
21:57.940 --> 21:59.790
Chen Yun gave a detailed account

423
21:59.880 --> 22:03.340
of the Long March of the Central Red Army as he had witnessed it,

424
22:03.750 --> 22:05.670
with particular emphasis on the expanded Politburo meeting

425
22:05.670 --> 22:08.160
held by the CPC Central Committee in Zunyi.

426
22:09.670 --> 22:12.600
Hearing about the major changes within the Party and the Red Army,

427
22:12.600 --> 22:15.400
Wang Ming was both surprised and uneasy.

428
22:16.270 --> 22:19.330
It seems the military strategy pursued by Comrade Bo Gu

429
22:19.710 --> 22:21.510
was not supported by the people.

430
22:22.880 --> 22:24.710
What I want to know now is

431
22:25.120 --> 22:28.250
the Central Committee's position on the political line

432
22:28.270 --> 22:30.800
adopted at the Fourth and Fifth Plenums

433
22:31.230 --> 22:33.030
of the Sixth Central Committee.

434
22:34.640 --> 22:36.230
During the Zunyi Conference,

435
22:36.230 --> 22:37.640
some comrades did indeed propose

436
22:37.640 --> 22:39.470
discussing the political line.

437
22:40.080 --> 22:43.270
But Comrade Mao Zedong did not agree.

438
22:43.510 --> 22:44.200
He believed

439
22:44.400 --> 22:47.160
that correcting the errors of the Party's military line

440
22:47.160 --> 22:48.860
was not about creating divisions within the Party,

441
22:48.860 --> 22:50.860
but about achieving greater unity.

442
22:50.930 --> 22:53.000
As Comrade Luofu wrote

443
22:53.030 --> 22:54.230
in the conference resolution,

444
22:54.230 --> 22:55.670
it was specifically stated

445
22:55.670 --> 22:58.670
that the Central Committee considered the political line pursued

446
22:58.670 --> 23:00.340
since the Fourth Plenum of the Sixth Central Committee

447
23:00.340 --> 23:02.360
to be unquestionably correct.

448
23:05.270 --> 23:07.270
The objectives of the Zunyi Conference were clear,

449
23:07.270 --> 23:09.270
and the discussions were thorough.

450
23:09.640 --> 23:12.120
What else was decided at the Zunyi Conference?

451
23:12.120 --> 23:14.640
Comrade Mao Zedong was added

452
23:14.670 --> 23:16.670
to the Politburo Standing Committee.

453
23:16.670 --> 23:19.880
It seems Comrade Mao Zedong

454
23:20.190 --> 23:22.560
has won everyone's unanimous support.

455
23:23.510 --> 23:25.170
Later, the Central Committee

456
23:25.400 --> 23:27.430
reached the border area of Yunnan, Guizhou, and Sichuan,

457
23:27.430 --> 23:29.360
where it held a Politburo meeting

458
23:29.400 --> 23:30.880
in a place called Jimingsansheng Village.

459
23:30.880 --> 23:32.430
At Comrade Mao Zedong's suggestion,

460
23:32.430 --> 23:34.710
Comrade Luofu replaced Comrade Bo Gu

461
23:34.750 --> 23:37.190
as the person in overall charge of the Central Committee.

462
23:37.190 --> 23:38.080
Is that so?

463
23:38.430 --> 23:40.400
Comrade Luofu took over as the person in charge?

464
23:40.400 --> 23:41.030
Yes.

465
23:41.640 --> 23:42.770
And what about Bo Gu?

466
23:42.800 --> 23:45.320
Comrade Bo Gu remained a member of the Politburo Standing Committee

467
23:45.320 --> 23:49.450
and was assigned to oversee the work of the General Political Department.

468
23:54.670 --> 23:55.670
Is the pear sweet?

469
23:55.840 --> 23:56.880
I still think

470
23:57.360 --> 23:59.400
the pears back home are sweeter.

471
24:00.670 --> 24:01.670
Comrade Chen Yun,

472
24:02.030 --> 24:03.320
in principle,

473
24:03.320 --> 24:05.920
I agree with the resolution of the Zunyi Conference.

474
24:05.920 --> 24:07.230
I'll arrange for you to meet

475
24:07.230 --> 24:08.950
Comrade Georgi Dimitrov as soon as possible,

476
24:08.950 --> 24:11.750
so you can brief him on the situation in person.

477
24:11.840 --> 24:12.800
All right.

478
24:13.320 --> 24:14.430
While I was in Shanghai,

479
24:14.430 --> 24:15.430
I also wrote an account entitled

480
24:15.430 --> 24:17.030
"An Eyewitness Account of the Red Army's Westward March."

481
24:17.030 --> 24:19.430
I plan to use this lengthy account as a basis

482
24:19.560 --> 24:21.960
for drafting a more comprehensive report.

483
24:22.120 --> 24:24.650
It seems you've made thorough preparations.

484
24:27.270 --> 24:28.120
And

485
24:28.510 --> 24:30.510
there's another piece of good news.

486
24:30.670 --> 24:31.990
The Comintern has just held

487
24:31.990 --> 24:33.590
its Seventh World Congress.

488
24:33.920 --> 24:34.800
I,

489
24:35.430 --> 24:36.600
Comrade Mao Zedong,

490
24:36.880 --> 24:38.140
Comrade Zhang Guotao,

491
24:38.230 --> 24:39.820
and Comrade Zhou Enlai were elected

492
24:39.820 --> 24:43.020
to the Executive Committee of the Comintern.

493
24:43.430 --> 24:46.510
Meanwhile, in response to the global anti-fascist movement

494
24:46.510 --> 24:48.640
and to promote the nationwide campaign to resist Japan and save the nation,

495
24:48.640 --> 24:49.840
we drafted a document

496
24:50.030 --> 24:52.320
which was then reviewed and approved

497
24:52.400 --> 24:53.840
at a meeting of the Secretariat

498
24:53.840 --> 24:55.080
of the Executive Committee of the Comintern.

499
24:55.080 --> 24:58.390
It was titled "A Message to All Compatriots on Resisting Japan and Saving the Nation

500
24:58.390 --> 25:01.920
from the Chinese Soviet Government and the CPC Central Committee."

501
25:01.920 --> 25:04.950
It came to be known as the "August 1 Declaration."

502
25:05.360 --> 25:08.120
We are about to send Comrade Lin Yuying back to China

503
25:08.120 --> 25:09.750
to convey the spirit of the 7th World Congress of the Comintern

504
25:09.750 --> 25:12.030
and the key points of the August 1 Declaration

505
25:12.030 --> 25:15.600
to our comrades back home.

506
25:16.030 --> 25:17.120
That's wonderful!

507
25:18.750 --> 25:21.400
Comrade Yuying, I wish you a safe and successful journey.

508
25:21.400 --> 25:22.120
Thank you.

509
25:22.930 --> 25:25.690
On October 15, 1935,

510
25:26.120 --> 25:28.270
at the invitation of the Comintern, Chen Yun gave a detailed account

511
25:28.270 --> 25:31.190
at a meeting of the Secretariat of the Executive Committee of the Comintern

512
25:31.190 --> 25:33.840
of the Long March of the Central Red Army

513
25:33.990 --> 25:35.400
and the Zunyi Conference

514
25:35.400 --> 25:37.600
held by the CPC.

515
25:38.230 --> 25:39.990
In his report, Chen Yun stated,

516
25:40.510 --> 25:43.040
"Our Party has certainly made some mistakes,

517
25:43.600 --> 25:46.200
but it corrected them through its own efforts.

518
25:46.270 --> 25:48.880
Our Party has truly matured.

519
25:49.360 --> 25:51.800
In particular, its leaders have matured.

520
25:52.160 --> 25:55.120
Military leaders such as Mao Zedong and Zhu De

521
25:55.190 --> 25:56.710
have now matured."

522
25:57.640 --> 25:58.670
After the meeting,

523
25:58.670 --> 26:01.920
someone compiled Chen Yun's report into a written document.

524
26:01.920 --> 26:04.450
Entitled "The Heroic Westward Expedition,"

525
26:04.510 --> 26:06.320
it was published in the spring of 1936

526
26:06.320 --> 26:08.080
in the magazine The Communist International,

527
26:08.080 --> 26:10.360
published by the Comintern.

528
26:10.560 --> 26:12.840
It became the earliest systematic account of the Red Army's Long March

529
26:12.840 --> 26:16.320
to be published in the international revolutionary camp.

530
26:19.350 --> 26:23.170
[Mount Emei, Sichuan]

531
26:21.200 --> 26:22.090
Generalissimo.

532
26:22.090 --> 26:23.600
Tonight's splendid gathering

533
26:23.600 --> 26:26.710
reminds me of a particularly fitting Tang poem.

534
26:27.360 --> 26:29.670
"From all corners of the realm, they gather here to pay homage to the sovereign.

535
26:29.670 --> 26:32.670
Beneath Mount Emei, the immortals take their place."

536
26:33.230 --> 26:34.640
I hardly deserve such praise.

537
26:34.640 --> 26:35.600
But that reminds me of 2 other lines

538
26:35.600 --> 26:37.880
from the same ten-poem cycle by Li Bai.

539
26:38.200 --> 26:40.150
"The Qin forged roads to Shu with golden oxen as its ruse.

540
26:40.150 --> 26:43.180
The Han River flows as though it joins the Milky Way."

541
26:43.390 --> 26:44.600
Yuanjing (He Guoguang).

542
26:44.600 --> 26:45.240
Yes, sir.

543
26:45.400 --> 26:46.470
Tell us,

544
26:46.560 --> 26:48.360
what does the golden ox refer to?

545
26:48.360 --> 26:49.160
The golden...

546
26:49.800 --> 26:51.050
The golden ox is Cixiu (Chen Cheng).

547
26:51.050 --> 26:51.520
No, no.

548
26:51.550 --> 26:52.700
I wouldn't dare.

549
26:53.950 --> 26:54.750
Gentlemen,

550
26:54.920 --> 26:57.080
you are all pillars of the Party.

551
26:57.160 --> 26:59.420
You are all golden oxen in your own right!

552
27:00.840 --> 27:01.990
Come on, take your seats.

553
27:01.990 --> 27:03.120
Please, have a seat.

554
27:03.470 --> 27:04.730
Zurong (Yan Daogang).

555
27:04.840 --> 27:06.320
Zurong, what is it?

556
27:06.360 --> 27:08.080
Generalissimo, I have an urgent military report

557
27:08.080 --> 27:09.270
that I must bring to your attention.

558
27:09.270 --> 27:10.670
According to aerial reconnaissance,

559
27:10.670 --> 27:11.880
a Communist force has been spotted

560
27:11.880 --> 27:13.880
in the area around the Bailong River, heading north.

561
27:13.880 --> 27:15.230
Its strength is estimated at fewer than ten thousand.

562
27:15.230 --> 27:16.680
Fewer than ten thousand heading north?

563
27:16.680 --> 27:17.990
Didn't they just join forces?

564
27:17.990 --> 27:19.510
Why have they split up so soon?

565
27:19.510 --> 27:20.630
If they're heading north,

566
27:20.630 --> 27:23.430
their destination may be Shaanxi and Gansu.

567
27:23.640 --> 27:27.400
In that case, the Communist troops will surely have to pass through Lazikou.

568
27:27.400 --> 27:28.330
Generalissimo.

569
27:28.560 --> 27:30.600
The route north from Sichuan into Shaanxi and Gansu passed through

570
27:30.600 --> 27:32.550
the stretch between E'jie and Minzhou,

571
27:32.550 --> 27:33.620
where a natural mountain pass known as Lazikou

572
27:33.620 --> 27:34.560
stood as a strategic gateway.

573
27:34.560 --> 27:36.160
The pass is about 30 meters deep,

574
27:36.160 --> 27:37.510
and only about 8 meters wide at its narrowest point.

575
27:37.510 --> 27:39.430
Steep cliffs rise on both sides,

576
27:39.430 --> 27:40.640
reaching heights of about 500 meters.

577
27:40.640 --> 27:41.640
Below lies the Lazi River,

578
27:41.640 --> 27:42.710
with its swift-flowing waters.

579
27:42.710 --> 27:43.990
The only way through the pass

580
27:43.990 --> 27:46.750
is via the single wooden bridge spanning the river.

581
27:46.750 --> 27:47.640
To ensure its security,

582
27:47.640 --> 27:49.380
two stone fortifications have also been built.

583
27:49.380 --> 27:50.670
It is easy to defend but difficult to attack.

584
27:50.670 --> 27:51.510
Good.

585
27:54.030 --> 27:55.710
Who is responsible for defending Lazikou?

586
27:55.710 --> 27:57.530
It falls under the jurisdiction of the Gansu Pacification Headquarters,

587
27:57.530 --> 27:58.640
commanded by Zhu Shaoliang.

588
27:58.640 --> 28:00.230
The actual defense arrangements are being handled by

589
28:00.230 --> 28:02.230
Lu Dachang of the 14th New Division.

590
28:02.750 --> 28:05.030
Generalissimo, I believe

591
28:05.120 --> 28:06.430
if this Communist force includes

592
28:06.430 --> 28:07.880
their central leadership,

593
28:07.880 --> 28:09.030
it would be

594
28:09.190 --> 28:10.880
an extraordinary opportunity for us.

595
28:10.880 --> 28:12.160
A stroke of great fortune.

596
28:12.160 --> 28:14.120
Send an urgent telegram to Zhu Shaoliang at once.

597
28:14.120 --> 28:15.640
Tell him to order Lu Dachang

598
28:15.640 --> 28:17.270
to hold Lazikou at all costs.

599
28:17.320 --> 28:17.850
Yes, sir.

600
28:17.880 --> 28:19.320
If what you say is true

601
28:19.560 --> 28:20.640
and we manage to kill key members of the CPC's high command

602
28:20.640 --> 28:23.430
at Lazikou,

603
28:23.710 --> 28:25.840
the bounty will be increased by five times.

604
28:25.840 --> 28:26.270
Yes, sir.

605
28:26.270 --> 28:27.880
Generalissimo, it's time.

606
28:27.920 --> 28:30.050
Everyone is waiting for your address.

607
28:30.400 --> 28:31.000
All right.

608
28:43.840 --> 28:45.270
My fellow comrades,

609
28:45.710 --> 28:46.880
good evening.

610
28:46.920 --> 28:48.670
Unity of purpose!

611
28:48.670 --> 28:50.920
Fraternity and sincerity!

612
28:54.990 --> 28:56.640
Everyone, attention!

613
28:57.120 --> 28:57.990
At ease!

614
29:01.880 --> 29:02.710
Everyone,

615
29:03.630 --> 29:06.430
today is the 16th day of the 8th lunar month

616
29:06.460 --> 29:08.720
in the 24th year of the Republic of China.

617
29:09.120 --> 29:11.030
Back in my hometown,

618
29:11.430 --> 29:13.510
we have a custom.

619
29:13.750 --> 29:15.880
We celebrate the Mid-Autumn Festival

620
29:15.950 --> 29:17.920
on the 16th day of the 8th lunar month.

621
29:17.920 --> 29:20.710
So tonight, here on Mount Emei,

622
29:20.950 --> 29:22.160
with all of you here

623
29:22.180 --> 29:24.110
to celebrate the festival with me,

624
29:24.160 --> 29:26.230
I am especially delighted.

625
29:31.750 --> 29:34.880
I wonder if any of you have noticed

626
29:35.080 --> 29:38.720
how exceptionally clear and bright the moon is tonight.

627
29:39.670 --> 29:40.800
The Mid-Autumn moon

628
29:41.990 --> 29:43.560
symbolizes completeness.

629
29:43.990 --> 29:45.670
Your successful graduation

630
29:45.920 --> 29:47.620
is also a form of completeness.

631
29:47.620 --> 29:50.310
What a rare and wonderful occasion this is!

632
29:50.880 --> 29:53.170
I hope you will remember tonight.

633
29:53.880 --> 29:56.080
Next year, the year after,

634
29:56.270 --> 29:57.840
and many years from now,

635
29:57.950 --> 29:59.610
when you look back on tonight,

636
29:59.840 --> 30:02.270
you will remember

637
30:02.400 --> 30:03.990
the gathering we shared.

638
30:04.230 --> 30:05.670
By then,

639
30:05.750 --> 30:09.140
you will realize just how meaningful it was.

640
30:10.470 --> 30:12.400
Let us raise our glasses together.

641
30:18.270 --> 30:20.920
May we all stand united in fraternity and sincerity,

642
30:20.920 --> 30:24.450
and may the Party's great campaign to eradicate the Communists

643
30:24.560 --> 30:27.470
be brought to a perfect conclusion!

644
30:28.880 --> 30:29.950
That's it!

645
30:30.270 --> 30:31.990
Unity of purpose!

646
30:32.030 --> 30:33.910
Fraternity and sincerity!

647
30:43.610 --> 30:47.800
[Outside Yongping Town, Yanchuan, Shaanxi]

648
30:49.840 --> 30:50.510
Han Xianchu.

649
30:50.510 --> 30:51.120
Here!

650
30:51.160 --> 30:52.510
Yongping Town is just ahead.

651
30:52.390 --> 30:53.990
[Han Xianchu, Company Commander, 1st Battalion, 225th Regiment, 25th Red Army]

652
30:52.600 --> 30:54.190
Tell everyone to look sharp!

653
30:54.070 --> 30:55.950
[Xu Haidong, Commander of the 25th Red Army]

654
30:54.270 --> 30:56.270
We must show them the spirit and fighting vigor

655
30:56.270 --> 30:57.160
of the 25th Red Army!

656
30:57.160 --> 30:57.920
Yes, sir!

657
30:59.120 --> 31:00.560
Heads up! Chests out!

658
31:00.640 --> 31:02.270
Stand tall!

659
31:02.270 --> 31:04.400
We represent the 25th Red Army.

660
31:03.340 --> 31:05.020
[Cheng Zihua, Political Commissar of the 25th Red Army]

661
31:04.510 --> 31:06.750
A Red Army soldier must look the part.

662
31:06.770 --> 31:07.850
Yes, sir!

663
31:07.990 --> 31:08.840
Han Xianchu!

664
31:08.950 --> 31:09.510
Here!

665
31:09.560 --> 31:10.430
Have everyone sing a verse!

666
31:10.430 --> 31:11.160
Yes, sir!

667
31:11.270 --> 31:15.030
♪ The young Red Army soldiers march with pride ♪

668
31:15.160 --> 31:16.990
Ready! Sing!

669
31:17.190 --> 31:21.430
♪ The young Red Army soldiers march with pride ♪

670
31:21.510 --> 31:25.400
♪ Like the rising sun in the east ♪

671
31:25.400 --> 31:29.400
♪ Fearless of sacrifice, we fight the enemy like tigers ♪

672
31:29.880 --> 31:30.600
Zihua,

673
31:30.990 --> 31:32.670
that's the spirit we're looking for!

674
31:32.670 --> 31:33.640
Right! That's the spirit!

675
31:33.640 --> 31:36.840
♪ We must study military affairs, politics, culture and recreation ♪

676
31:36.950 --> 31:41.230
♪ We will become the masters of tomorrow ♪

677
31:42.120 --> 31:43.530
Zihua, let's go!

678
31:44.060 --> 31:44.890
Let's go!

679
31:44.990 --> 31:49.470
♪ We will become the masters of tomorrow ♪

680
31:53.330 --> 31:56.530
[Liu Zhidan, Chairman of the Northwest Revolutionary Military Commission]

681
31:54.470 --> 31:55.950
Which one of you is Comrade Xu Haidong?

682
31:55.950 --> 31:57.120
I'm Liu Zhidan.

683
32:01.510 --> 32:02.670
I'm Xu Haidong.

684
32:02.710 --> 32:03.920
Comrade Liu Zhidan.

685
32:04.230 --> 32:05.230
I finally get to meet you!

686
32:05.230 --> 32:06.640
Good to meet you, Comrade Haidong.

687
32:06.640 --> 32:07.750
Allow me to introduce you.

688
32:07.750 --> 32:09.750
This is our political commissar, Comrade Cheng Zihua.

689
32:09.750 --> 32:10.670
Good to meet you, Comrade Zhidan.

690
32:10.670 --> 32:11.600
Good to meet you, Comrade Zihua.

691
32:11.600 --> 32:13.330
As soon as we got word from Comrade Zhongxun,

692
32:13.330 --> 32:14.400
our 26th and 27th Armies

693
32:14.400 --> 32:16.640
made straight for Yongping Town without stopping.

694
32:16.640 --> 32:19.270
The whole town has now been mobilized.

695
32:19.470 --> 32:22.400
We're just waiting to join forces with the 25th Army.

696
32:22.560 --> 32:23.840
I'm an impatient man,

697
32:23.950 --> 32:24.950
so I came straight out to meet you.

698
32:24.950 --> 32:25.880
Then we're alike.

699
32:25.880 --> 32:26.940
I'm impatient too.

700
32:27.710 --> 32:28.670
Comrade Zhidan,

701
32:28.850 --> 32:30.000
you've made us feel

702
32:30.030 --> 32:31.560
the warmth of brotherhood.

703
32:31.640 --> 32:32.840
Our 25th Army

704
32:32.990 --> 32:35.520
has fought its way here, battle after battle,

705
32:35.670 --> 32:37.200
through untold hardships.

706
32:38.430 --> 32:40.430
And now, we've finally made it home.

707
32:40.430 --> 32:41.950
That's right. You're home.

708
32:41.950 --> 32:44.350
From now on, our 2 forces will join together

709
32:44.430 --> 32:46.140
to build this revolutionary base area.

710
32:46.140 --> 32:46.770
Well said!

711
32:46.800 --> 32:47.510
Excellent!

712
32:47.920 --> 32:48.850
Comrade Zhidan,

713
32:49.320 --> 32:51.320
have you heard anything about the Central Red Army?

714
32:51.320 --> 32:52.270
Nothing so far.

715
32:52.360 --> 32:54.230
But according to enemy newspapers,

716
32:54.230 --> 32:56.270
the Central Red Army should be heading north,

717
32:56.270 --> 32:57.950
making its way toward us.

718
32:58.430 --> 32:59.260
Then we came the right way.

719
32:59.260 --> 32:59.790
Exactly!

720
33:00.230 --> 33:01.030
Wonderful!

721
33:05.360 --> 33:07.190
Comrades of the 25th Red Army,

722
33:07.510 --> 33:09.920
welcome to the Shaanxi-Gansu Revolutionary Base Area!

723
33:09.920 --> 33:11.190
All right!

724
33:11.270 --> 33:13.360
Everyone, this way!

725
33:13.430 --> 33:14.640
All right!

726
33:14.670 --> 33:18.510
♪ The young Red Army soldiers march with pride ♪

727
33:18.670 --> 33:22.400
♪ Like the rising sun in the east ♪

728
33:22.470 --> 33:26.360
♪ Fearless of sacrifice, we fight the enemy like tigers ♪

729
33:26.360 --> 33:29.470
♪ We charge into battle, pressing forward, unstoppable ♪

730
33:29.470 --> 33:31.880
On September 16, 1935,

731
33:32.070 --> 33:34.470
the 25th Red Army successfully joined forces with the 26th Red Army

732
33:34.470 --> 33:35.710
and the 27th Red Army

733
33:35.860 --> 33:39.100
in Yongping Town, Yanchuan County.

734
33:39.670 --> 33:41.060
Following the Yongping reunion,

735
33:41.060 --> 33:44.510
the CPC Northwest Working Committee and the CPC Hubei-Henan-Shaanxi Provincial Committee

736
33:44.510 --> 33:46.880
held a joint meeting in Yongping Town.

737
33:47.400 --> 33:49.230
They decided to abolish their separate organizational structures

738
33:49.230 --> 33:52.560
and jointly establish the CPC Shaanxi-Gansu-Shanxi Provincial Committee.

739
33:52.560 --> 33:54.510
The designations of the 25th, 26th

740
33:54.510 --> 33:56.230
and 27th Red Armies were abolished.

741
33:56.230 --> 33:59.780
The Chinese Workers' and Peasants' Red Army's 15th Corps was formed.

742
33:59.780 --> 34:01.950
Xu Haidong was appointed Corps Commander,

743
34:01.950 --> 34:04.010
Cheng Zihua, Political Commissar,

744
34:04.270 --> 34:07.530
and Liu Zhidan, Deputy Corps Commander and Chief of Staff.

745
34:07.560 --> 34:09.400
Since leaving the Hubei-Henan-Anhui Revolutionary

746
34:09.400 --> 34:11.320
Base Area in November 1934,

747
34:11.320 --> 34:13.239
the 25th Red Army had operated

748
34:13.239 --> 34:15.400
without any contact with the Central Committee.

749
34:15.400 --> 34:17.400
It had made its own decisions and conducted its own operations

750
34:17.400 --> 34:18.699
over a period of 10 months,

751
34:18.699 --> 34:20.409
covering nearly 5,000 kilometers

752
34:20.409 --> 34:22.010
across Hubei, Henan,

753
34:22.320 --> 34:23.630
Shaanxi and Gansu.

754
34:23.920 --> 34:26.250
It had fought in more than 20 major battles

755
34:26.429 --> 34:27.719
and repelled encirclement and pursuit campaigns by

756
34:27.719 --> 34:29.760
over 30 regiments of the KMT troops.

757
34:30.070 --> 34:32.800
It had established the Hubei-Henan-Shaanxi Revolutionary Base Area

758
34:32.800 --> 34:33.900
and became the first Red Army unit

759
34:33.900 --> 34:36.690
on the Long March to reach northern Shaanxi.

760
34:36.989 --> 34:38.989
Mao Zedong later remarked:

761
34:39.130 --> 34:42.380
Xu Haidong's journey from southern Shaanxi, through eastern Gansu, into northern Shaanxi

762
34:42.380 --> 34:45.560
had, by sheer coincidence, made him a guide for the Central Red Army.

763
34:45.560 --> 34:46.510
After the E'jie Conference,

764
34:46.510 --> 34:48.070
the situation grew increasingly grave.

765
34:48.070 --> 34:50.150
To avoid being cut off by the KMT troops,

766
34:50.150 --> 34:52.469
the Central Red Army led the main force of the 1st Front Red Army

767
34:52.469 --> 34:53.469
northward.

768
34:53.590 --> 34:55.989
On September 16, 1935,

769
34:56.110 --> 34:58.360
it arrived at Heiduo Temple

770
34:58.400 --> 34:59.510
in what is now Diebu County, Gansu Province.

771
34:59.510 --> 35:01.070
At Heiduo Temple,

772
35:01.070 --> 35:02.880
Mao Zedong, together with Lin Biao and Nie Rongzhen,

773
35:02.880 --> 35:04.320
devised a battle plan

774
35:04.320 --> 35:07.520
to win the decisive battle for entry into southern Gansu.

775
35:07.550 --> 35:09.880
The goal was to seize the natural fortress of Lazikou.

776
35:09.880 --> 35:10.960
The latest enemy intelligence.

777
35:10.960 --> 35:14.470
[Heiduo Temple, Heila, Gansu]

778
35:11.200 --> 35:12.550
Lu Dachang has sent his elite

779
35:12.550 --> 35:14.280
1st Brigade, consisting of 3 regiments,

780
35:14.280 --> 35:15.110
to Lazikou.

781
35:15.280 --> 35:16.800
Besides guarding the natural fortress at Lazikou,

782
35:16.800 --> 35:18.550
they have also established multiple lines of defense

783
35:18.550 --> 35:20.110
between the pass and Minzhou.

784
35:20.110 --> 35:21.380
What do you propose?

785
35:21.030 --> 35:26.120
[Nie Rongzhen, Political Commissar of the 1st Red Army; Lin Biao, Commander of the 1st Red Army]

786
35:22.710 --> 35:23.570
Our only option

787
35:23.590 --> 35:25.360
is to capture Lazikou as soon as possible,

788
35:25.360 --> 35:26.720
whatever the cost.

789
35:27.240 --> 35:29.070
Your resolve is right.

790
35:29.510 --> 35:32.590
If we fail to break through the natural fortress at Lazikou soon,

791
35:32.590 --> 35:33.590
the Shaanxi-Gansu Detachment

792
35:33.590 --> 35:36.150
will have no choice but to turn back into the grasslands.

793
35:36.150 --> 35:37.720
And then we'll face

794
35:37.720 --> 35:41.250
a massive encirclement campaign by dozens of enemy regiments.

795
35:42.040 --> 35:43.030
Which unit will take on the mission

796
35:43.030 --> 35:43.920
of breaking through Lazikou?

797
35:43.920 --> 35:45.250
The 4th Regiment again.

798
35:45.590 --> 35:47.510
The political commissar and I will head there at once.

799
35:47.510 --> 35:47.990
Good.

800
35:48.110 --> 35:49.950
I'll be waiting for news of your victory.

801
35:49.950 --> 35:50.840
I have every confidence

802
35:50.840 --> 35:52.510
that the 4th Regiment, which seized the Luding Bridge in a lightning assault,

803
35:52.510 --> 35:54.630
can also overcome the natural fortress of Lazikou.

804
35:54.630 --> 35:55.070
Yes, sir!

805
35:55.070 --> 35:55.600
Yes, sir!

806
36:01.750 --> 36:06.610
[Lazikou, Gansu]

807
36:32.160 --> 36:36.040
[Lazikou, Gansu; Temporary Headquarters of the 4th Regiment]

808
36:44.590 --> 36:45.200
Messenger.

809
36:45.200 --> 36:45.680
Here!

810
36:47.630 --> 36:48.710
Order the 1st Company of the 1st Battalion

811
36:48.710 --> 36:49.340
to conduct a reconnaissance by fire.

812
36:49.340 --> 36:50.020
Yes, sir!

813
37:30.510 --> 37:32.570
[Mao Zhenhua, Commander of the 1st Company, 1st Battalion, 4th Regiment]

814
37:41.720 --> 37:42.590
Fire!

815
38:08.030 --> 38:10.030
[Yang Chengwu, Political Commissar of the 4th Regiment]

816
38:21.570 --> 38:24.500
[Huang Kaixiang, Commander of the 4th Regiment]

817
38:51.280 --> 38:52.430
Take cover!

818
38:56.990 --> 38:58.650
You Communist Army soldiers!

819
38:58.950 --> 38:59.990
Go back!

820
39:00.800 --> 39:03.060
Don't come here to throw your lives away!

821
39:03.200 --> 39:04.680
You'll never get through!

822
39:05.280 --> 39:06.360
Send one of your men,

823
39:06.240 --> 39:09.640
[Zhang Jueseng, Chief of Staff of the 1st Brigade, 14th New Division of the KMT Troops]

824
39:06.590 --> 39:07.880
and I'll kill one!

825
39:08.400 --> 39:09.400
Send two,

826
39:10.130 --> 39:11.730
and I'll kill them both!

827
39:14.240 --> 39:15.110
Open fire!

828
39:15.240 --> 39:16.360
Kill them all!

829
39:23.970 --> 39:24.850
Fall back!

830
39:25.700 --> 39:26.490
Move!

831
39:44.150 --> 39:46.030
This is much harder than crossing the Luding Bridge.

832
39:46.030 --> 39:47.070
It sure is hard.

833
39:47.470 --> 39:49.430
At Luding Bridge, we could force our way across. Here, we can't.

834
39:49.430 --> 39:50.720
Even two 4th Regiments wouldn't make it across

835
39:50.720 --> 39:53.200
the open ground at the end of the bridge under enemy fire.

836
39:53.200 --> 39:54.200
Political Commissar Yang!

837
39:54.200 --> 39:55.730
Regiment Commander Huang!

838
39:57.180 --> 39:58.180
Section Chief Li.

839
40:00.840 --> 40:01.840
Section Chief Li.

840
40:01.920 --> 40:02.920
What brings you up here?

841
40:02.920 --> 40:04.110
The situation is critical.

842
40:04.110 --> 40:06.630
We must break through Lazikou before dawn tomorrow.

843
40:06.630 --> 40:08.630
The army commander, political commissar, and Division Commander Chen Guang are all here.

844
40:08.630 --> 40:09.760
They're down the mountain.

845
40:09.760 --> 40:12.420
They want to see the 4th Regiment's battle plan.

846
40:16.430 --> 40:18.620
Section Chief Li, please tell the leaders

847
40:18.620 --> 40:20.400
that we're working on a battle plan right now.

848
40:20.400 --> 40:21.330
Once it's ready,

849
40:21.360 --> 40:22.470
we'll report to them immediately.

850
40:22.470 --> 40:24.320
You know what the army commander is like.

851
40:24.320 --> 40:25.430
Let me remind you,

852
40:26.030 --> 40:26.840
there's no time to waste.

853
40:26.840 --> 40:27.630
-Yes. -Yes.

854
40:35.200 --> 40:36.030
It's clear

855
40:36.240 --> 40:37.470
that the leaders don't want to hear

856
40:37.470 --> 40:38.880
about a reckless frontal assault at any cost.

857
40:38.880 --> 40:39.840
Yang, you don't need to remind me.

858
40:39.840 --> 40:41.200
I know a battle takes brains.

859
40:41.200 --> 40:42.340
But look at this terrain.

860
40:42.340 --> 40:43.320
It's simply not the kind of place

861
40:43.320 --> 40:44.220
where clever tactics can get us anywhere.

862
40:44.220 --> 40:45.760
You need to keep calm, Huang.

863
40:45.760 --> 40:46.200
If you don't keep calm...

864
40:46.200 --> 40:48.000
Aren't you losing your cool too?

865
40:50.090 --> 40:50.690
All right.

866
40:51.240 --> 40:52.440
Let's both calm down.

867
40:52.590 --> 40:54.880
In theory, no battle is unwinnable.

868
40:55.030 --> 40:56.000
I know.

869
40:56.030 --> 40:58.350
Chairman Mao said we must fight with flexibility and mobility,

870
40:58.350 --> 41:00.200
and look for the enemy's weak points.

871
41:00.200 --> 41:02.110
But Yang, think it through carefully.

872
41:02.110 --> 41:03.550
Does enemy here have any weak points at all?

873
41:03.550 --> 41:05.320
That's exactly why we have to look for them.

874
41:05.320 --> 41:06.000
Right.

875
41:06.800 --> 41:08.360
They have solid fortifications

876
41:08.360 --> 41:09.760
and plenty of firepower.

877
41:09.880 --> 41:11.950
As for us, we're short on heavy weapons,

878
41:11.950 --> 41:13.680
and the terrain is against us.

879
41:14.070 --> 41:14.760
But...

880
41:33.430 --> 41:35.630
Those bastards' bunkers have no roofs!

881
41:35.710 --> 41:37.380
Yang, look. Look!

882
41:38.200 --> 41:39.800
Their bunkers have no roofs!

883
41:46.690 --> 41:48.270
They're just using the cliffs to their advantage,

884
41:48.270 --> 41:49.820
thinking they don't need roofs at all.

885
41:49.820 --> 41:52.380
Notify all the companies to hold a "Zhuge Liang meeting".

886
41:52.380 --> 41:54.780
Let's put our heads together and find a way.

887
41:58.430 --> 41:59.290
Keep up! Hurry!

888
41:59.290 --> 42:01.000
Move! Move! Quick!

889
42:02.100 --> 42:02.840
Where's your company commander?

890
42:02.840 --> 42:03.500
Over there.

891
42:05.650 --> 42:07.250
Mao, come here.

892
42:09.320 --> 42:10.320
How did it go?

893
42:10.950 --> 42:11.950
Six wounded.

894
42:12.250 --> 42:12.870
Not bad.

895
42:12.920 --> 42:13.880
Not bad, my foot!

896
42:14.800 --> 42:16.110
If we keep fighting like this,

897
42:16.110 --> 42:17.640
we'll all be sitting ducks.

898
42:17.880 --> 42:19.030
I know you're worried,

899
42:19.030 --> 42:20.240
but what else can we do?

900
42:20.240 --> 42:21.280
We can't exactly fly over the pass.

901
42:21.280 --> 42:22.030
Don't worry?

902
42:22.400 --> 42:24.070
How can I not be worried in a situation like this?

903
42:24.070 --> 42:25.290
How much time do we have left?

904
42:25.290 --> 42:26.400
Up front, they had us pinned down so badly

905
42:26.400 --> 42:27.760
that we couldn't even lift our heads!

906
42:27.760 --> 42:28.820
It's humiliating!

907
42:29.030 --> 42:31.360
Company Commander, can I say something?

908
42:32.720 --> 42:33.400
Go ahead.

909
42:34.320 --> 42:36.720
Company Commander, the bunkers have no roofs.

910
42:36.720 --> 42:38.120
I know they have no roofs.

911
42:38.150 --> 42:39.280
Do you have a mortar?

912
42:39.520 --> 42:40.360
Then why not climb to the top of the mountain

913
42:40.360 --> 42:41.880
and throw grenades down at them?

914
42:41.880 --> 42:42.720
Yun Guichuan,

915
42:43.110 --> 42:44.240
this mountain is nothing but bare rock.

916
42:44.240 --> 42:45.150
How are you supposed to climb it?

917
42:45.150 --> 42:47.080
If you can't make it up there, I can!

918
42:47.760 --> 42:49.150
I've been gathering medicinal herbs in the mountains since I was a boy.

919
42:49.150 --> 42:51.070
Climbing a mountain like this is a piece of cake for me.

920
42:51.070 --> 42:52.120
I'll climb up first,

921
42:52.120 --> 42:53.150
then lower a rope down to you.

922
42:53.150 --> 42:54.680
Wouldn't that do the trick?

923
42:54.990 --> 42:57.120
Company Commander, I really can do it!

924
42:58.240 --> 42:58.950
Go on.

925
43:00.150 --> 43:00.680
Let's go.

926
43:00.700 --> 43:01.030
Yes, sir!

927
43:01.030 --> 43:01.840
Let's give it a try.
